rd\nHubert Schenck Memorial Scholarship\nBob Compton Award\nEPS Bedrock Award\nOutstanding Undergraduate Award\nAdditional 2026 Awards and Recognitions\nPeople\nFaculty\nAssociated Faculty\nEmeritus\nLecturers\nResearchers / Lab Managers\nPostdocs\nGraduate Students\nUndergraduate Students\nStaff\nApply\nSupport\nApply|Support\nClose Menu\nAcademics\nResearch\nImpact\nExternal Education\nNews & Events\nAbout\nAcademics\nThe Stanford Doerr School of Sustainability educates the next generation of leaders to solve our greatest sustainability challenges. Through degree programs spanning engineering, Earth system and planetary science, energy science, social sciences, geophysics, and oceans, students learn, research, and collaborate both on campus and at field sites around the world.\nAcademics\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nPostdoctoral Resources\nDepartments and Programs\nDepartment of Civil & Environmental Engineering\nDepartment of Earth & Planetary Sciences\nDepartment of Earth System Science\nDepartment of Energy Science & Engineering\nDepartment of Environmental Social Sciences\nDepartment of Geophysics\nDepartment of Oceans\nEarth Systems Program\nEmmett Interdisciplinary Program in Environment & Resources\nChange Leadership for Sustainability Program (SUST)\nStudent Resources & Experience\nStudent Experience\nProfessional Development\nField Education\nAccess, Belonging and Community\nCareer Studio\nResearch\nScholars at the Stanford Doerr School of Sustainability focus on discovery and applied research essential for understanding our world and ensuring a thriving future. Through dedicated funding opportunities and access to cutting-edge facilities, including Hopkins Marine Station on Monterey Bay and the O'Donohue Family Stanford Educational Farm, they pursue bold ideas and turn science into real-world impact.\nResearch Topics\nResearch\nBiodiversity\nCities & Infrastructure\nClimate\nEarth & Planets\nEnergy\nHazards\nLand & Water\nSociety & Policy\nFunding Opportunities\nDiscovery Grants\nEngagement Grants\nPrecourt Institute Grants\nSolution Area Grants\nSustainability Accelerator Grants\nWoods Institute Grants\nView All\nCutting-Edge Facilities\nBranner Earth Sciences Library\nComputing Resources\nGeospatial Center\nHarold A. Miller Library\nHopkins Marine Station\nO'Donohue Family Stanford Educational Farm\nShared Labs\nImpact\nThe Stanford Doerr School of Sustainability launched in 2022 as Stanford's first new school in 75 years, bringing together disciplines to advance the long-term prosperity of humanity and the planet. From making electricity affordable and sustainable for all to designing cities where people and nature thrive, our scholars collaborate across Stanford and the world to build a better future.\nInstitutes\nPrecourt Institute for Energy\nWoods Institute for the Environment\nSustainability Accelerator\nAbout\nProjects\nTomKat Center\nSpinouts\nCenters, Programs and Initiatives\nWoods Institute for the Environment\nPrecourt Insitute for Energy\nSustainable Societies initiative\nIndustrial Affiliates Programs\nExternal Education\nTo shape a more sustainable world, the Stanford Doerr School of Sustainability extends learning opportunities and collaboration to students, scholars, solvers, and scalers across the globe. Opportunities include Executive Education, the Sustainability Forum, the Global Sustainability Challenge, Sustainability Undergraduate Research in Geoscience and Engineering, K-12 outreach, and Art and Sustainability.\nExternal & Executive Education\nPrograms for Individuals\nSelf-Paced Online Learning\nPrograms for Organizations\nDoerr School for the World\nArt & Sustainability\nGlobal Sustainability Challenge\nK-12 Outreach\nSustainability Undergraduate Research in Geoscience and Engineering Program\nSustainability Forum\n2026 Forum\nHighlights\nNews & Events\nDiscover the latest research and insights shaping the future of sustainability. From groundbreaking research and inspiring milestones, to global forums that bring scholars, students, and leaders together, the Stanford Doerr School of Sustainability is a catalyst for innovation, turning bold ideas into lasting impact.\nView all news\nResearch News\nBiodiversity\nCities & infrastructure\nClimate\nEarth & planets\nEnergy\nHazards\nLand & water\nSociety & policy\nAll research news topics\nLatest research stories\nSchool News\nCommunity\nLearning experiences\nProfiles\nPrograms & partnerships\nAll school news topics\nLatest school stories\nMore\nSubscribe\nResources for journalists\nIn the media\nUpcoming events\nAbout\nThe Stanford Doerr School of Sustainability advances knowledge, solutions, and impact through research and education, creating a thriving, enduring future for humanity and the planet. Its seven departments, two institutes, and Sustainability Accelerator work in concert. Institutes spark innovative environmental and energy research across disciplines, and the Accelerator turns research into scalable technology and policy solutions for urgent global challenges.\nLeadership & Community\nDean's Office\nFaculty\nStudents\nAdvisory Council\nAlumni\nAwards\nHistory\nHistory\nFoundational Launch Partners\nReturn to Site Menu\nAcademics\nAcademics\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nPostdoctoral Resources\nDepartments and Programs\nDepartment of Civil & Environmental Engineering\nDepartment of Earth & Planetary Sciences\nDepartment of Earth System Science\nDepartment of Energy Science & Engineering\nDepartment of Environmental Social Sciences\nDepartment of Geophysics\nDepartment of Oceans\nEarth Systems Program\nEmmett Interdisciplinary Program in Environment & Resources\nChange Leadership for Sustainability Program (SUST)\nStudent Resources & Experience\nStudent Experience\nProfessional Development\nField Education\nAccess, Belonging and Community\nCareer Studio\nResearch\nResearch Topics\nResearch\nBiodiversity\nCities & Infrastructure\nClimate\nEarth & Planets\nEnergy\nHazards\nLand & Water\nSociety & Policy\nFunding Opportunities\nDiscovery Grants\nEngagement Grants\nPrecourt Institute Grants\nSolution Area Grants\nSustainability Accelerator Grants\nWoods Institute Grants\nView All\nCutting-Edge Facilities\nBranner Earth Sciences Library\nComputing Resources\nGeospatial Center\nHarold A. Miller Library\nHopkins Marine Station\nO'Donohue Family Stanford Educational Farm\nShared Labs\nImpact\nInstitutes\nPrecourt Institute for Energy\nWoods Institute for the Environment\nSustainability Accelerator\nAbout\nProjects\nTomKat Center\nSpinouts\nCenters, Programs and Initiatives\nWoods Institute for the Environment\nPrecourt Insitute for Energy\nSustainable Societies initiative\nIndustrial Affiliates Programs\nExternal Education\nExternal & Executive Education\nPrograms for Individuals\nSelf-Paced Online Learning\nPrograms for Organizations\nDoerr School for the World\nArt & Sustainability\nGlobal Sustainability Challenge\nK-12 Outreach\nSustainability Undergraduate Research in Geoscience and Engineering Program\nSustainability Forum\n2026 Forum\nHighlights\nNews & Events\nView all news\nResearch News\nBiodiversity\nCities & infrastructure\nClimate\nEarth & planets\nEnergy\nHazards\nLand & water\nSociety & policy\nAll research news topics\nLatest research stories\nSchool News\nCommunity\nLearning experiences\nProfiles\nPrograms & partnerships\nAll school news topics\nLatest school stories\nMore\nSubscribe\nResources for journalists\nIn the media\nUpcoming events\nAbout\nLeadership & Community\nDean's Office\nFaculty\nStudents\nAdvisory Council\nAlumni\nAwards\nHistory\nHistory\nFoundational Launch Partners\nApply\nSupport\nExplore our Program\nSpacer\nSpacer\nAcademics & Admissions\nAcademics & Admissions\nWhy major in Earth and Planetary Sciences\nUndergraduate Program\nUndergraduate Program\nHonors Program\nResearch Opportunities\nGraduate Program\nGraduate Program\nApplication Information\nExplore our Program\nAdmission FAQs\nCoterminal MS Program\nThe Department of Earth and Planetary Sciences (EPS) offers Ph.D. and M.S. programs in a wide range of fields, including surface processes, geomorphology, geomechanics, structural and regional geology, tectonics, sedimentary geology and basin analysis, life and planetary evolution, petrology, geochemistry, mineralogy and mineral physics, environmental geology, geochronology and thermochronology, and geostatistics. The breadth of research in the department provide numerous opportunities for field-based research, laboratory and numerical experiments, modern applications of instrumental analysis and spectroscopy to problems in the earth sciences.\nSpacer\nExplore our dynamic research areas\nFaculty in the EPS department interact closely with other departments at Stanford, including Civil and Environmental, Mechanical, and Chemical Engineering, Chemistry, Biology, Statistics, and Applied Physics. Close collaborations with industry include the Monterey Bay Aquarium Research Institute, the Center for Materials Research, the Stanford Synchrotron Radiation Laboratory, and the U.S. Geological Survey. Students are encouraged to draw upon interdisciplinary projects. Complimentary programs are provided in the Departments of Geophysics, Energy Science & Engineering, and Earth System Science. See the list of programs within the Doerr School of Sustainability.\nSpacer\nExplore our research areas\nSpacer\nGet to know our faculty\nGet Involved\nFollow Us\nContact Us\nVisit Us\nQuick Links\nUpcoming events\nMake a gift\nOpen staff positions\nOpen faculty positions\nIntranet\nLogin\nWebsite feedback\nLearn more\nDepartments and Programs\nStanford Woods Institute for the Environment\nPrecourt Institute for Energy\nSustainability Accelerator\nStanford land acknowledgement\n\u00a9Stanford University.\nStanford, California 94305\nStanford Home\nMaps & Directions\nSearch Stanford\nEmergency Info\nTerms of Use\nPrivacy\nCopyright\nTrademarks\nNon-Discrimination\nAccessibility\nClose\nBio\nWebsite\nIG\nAbout\nPr